  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a persistent upward bias relative to true outcomes, consistently underestimating volatility and over-smoothing price reversals.",
    "When sentiment history shows low or zero values (0.00), the model fails to capture sudden mean-reversion spikes, resulting in significant negative errors during sharp drops followed by recoveries.",
    "The model demonstrates a lag in reacting to recent high prices; it extrapolates slowly upward while true outcomes often spike immediately after a period of consolidation.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate the magnitude of V-shaped recovery patterns where sentiment remains neutral but price action reverses direction abruptly.",
    "In scenarios with mixed sentiment (0.20/0.40), the model's linear projection fails to account for non-linear volatility expansion, leading to underestimated high-water marks."
  ]
}
